If I can re-hijack this thread, I started with SLASH'EM about the same
time (around a month ago), and just wanted to put my two bits in. I
played a lot of droven necromancers and Ice Mages at first, until I
figured out I was just getting destroyed with spellcasters. Killed off
a couple of combat-wombats and vampires, then tried random characters,
got a doppleganger monk, and fell in love - their technique
combinations are great.

I haven't been as deep as level 23 - I foolishly took on Master Kaen
with a promising character, got stoned _twice_ by hitting an "S" with
no gloves (an asphynx both times), and once lit a torch without
realizing I was _wielding_ it - got creamed by some low-level
beasties.

I've finished Sokoban and the Mines on probably 8 games, finished the
Lawful/Neutral/Chaotic quests a few times, and cleaned out Grund's
three or four times.

I've really enjoyed playing with some of the new stuff - monks stink
with most weapons, but dopplegangers apparently have an affinity for
firearms. Frag grenades are fun, as are wands of fireball. All in all,
I've been enjoying the new ideas, even if progress is slower than in
vanilla.

